{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war","id":1391093,"title":"second titan war","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-23T18:55:22-07:00","id":1391093,"title":"second titan war","content":"(long time reader, first time poster) <br /> <br /> I have some problems with 2nd ed of scion. I don't really like the changes. namely, the dis-unified cosmology. In 1st ed the titans were free and a unified threat, and the pantheons actually made semse. I don't get most of the new metaphysics. Why are the titanspawn acting up now, enough so that they are a problem. In 1st ed the titans were all imprisoned in the same place, and when something broke them free the gods needed to make scions so the war could be fought. But here the titans are still bound. <br /> <br /> so can someone help me make sense of why the second titan war has started in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T19:27:19-07:00","id":1391104,"title":"","content":"Well, I think a lot of that is left up to the individual game master, but my idea of the &quot;first Titan war,&quot; at least as I understand it, is that it was never really a singular event. It simply consisted of all the divine conflicts that occurred in the mythologies of each individual pantheon, all of which ended very distinctly from one another. Some pantheons vanquished their Titans or sealed them away, some formed truces with them or even accepted them into their rosters, some have Titans who remain thorns in their sides until today. There are also plenty of pantheons whose Titans were never in direct conflict with the gods to begin with, or don't even have figures which they consider to be Titans at all. The way I personally interpret the resurgence of malevolent Titanic activity is due to an inter-pantheon group of divine/titanic antagonists (essentially a mythical legion of doom) going around and resurrecting/freeing as many mythological big bads as possible to destroy all the pantheons in one fell swoop. The &quot;second titan war&quot; would actually be the first time all of the pantheons would have to form a united front against the Titans, as this would be the first time most of them were under siege all at once. Up until this point, the pantheons largely weren't too fond of each other, and the big &quot;epic quest&quot; of my campaign will involve having to go around and convince them all to join forces, with all the chaotic divine politics that would entail, and ultimately take part in the battle to end all battles against the cosmic threat.<br /> <br /> The other thing you should probably understand is that a unified cosmology and &quot;all myths are true&quot; are pretty much incompatible ideas, unless things are painted with unbelievably broad strokes, and, honestly, 2e paints it in very broad strokes regardless. 1e basically attempted to put all of the pantheons into a Greek/Nordic model of a divine conflict, which involved tons of square pegs in round holes. 2e doesn't try to take a singular formula to all of world mythology, which means the myths can be portrayed a lot more genuinely than 1e did. It involves a lot less forcing of mythical figures into roles that don't work for them, and, frankly, is a lot more respectful of the cultures they come from. Imo, I think it is a much better take on the source material, adhering to the letter and spirit of the stories in a far superior way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 05-23-2020, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T19:32:30-07:00","id":1391105,"title":"","content":"I like those ideas of a mythic league of doom and this being the first time the pantheons have to unite. <br /> <br /> but I love the 1st ed verson of the titans. and I honestly like 1st ed better. the first title of this thread was I like 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T22:54:27-07:00","id":1391133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war#post1391093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(long time reader, first time poster) <br /> <br /> I have some problems with 2nd ed of scion. I don't really like the changes. namely, the dis-unified cosmology. In 1st ed the titans were free and a unified threat, and the pantheons actually made semse. I don't get most of the new metaphysics. Why are the titanspawn acting up now, enough so that they are a problem. In 1st ed the titans were all imprisoned in the same place, and when something broke them free the gods needed to make scions so the war could be fought. But here the titans are still bound. <br /> <br /> so can someone help me make sense of why the second titan war has started in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>My answer: climate change is devastating the bonds of the Titan prisons in the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T02:20:19-07:00","id":1391149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391133#post1391133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My answer: climate change is devastating the bonds of the Titan prisons in the World.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not know what will be canon answer in <b>Titanomachy </b>book - but I LOVE this answer sssoooo much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T07:23:41-07:00","id":1391190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391149#post1391149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know what will be canon answer in <b>Titanomachy </b>book - but I LOVE this answer sssoooo much!</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like the climate change answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:07:59-07:00","id":1391256,"title":"","content":"The Titans in 1e ranged from &quot;Dumb&quot; to &quot;Nonsensical&quot; to &quot;Actively Offensive In Their Portrayals&quot; and 2e is better for having thrown the Greater Titan-Bodies With Titan Avatars into a bin, where they belong.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't go with the &quot;The Titans were bound&quot; because it takes a three-second moment of thinking to realize that this is a hecking lie, and that in fact if you're not of the Theoi a LOT of your Titans aren't bound at all. Ask Ra how well the Titans are bound, but make sure to ask during the day because otherwise literally all the Netjer will be fighting off... *Checks notes* A Titan.<br /> <br /> Ask any of the Teotl how well THEIR Titans are bound and they'll probably laugh at you before gearing up fro ANOTHER night of keeping the star demons from eating the sun.<br /> <br /> The Deva may just LOOK at you and go &quot;Bound how? Now if you'll excuse me, Durga needs to destroy another hundred thousand Asura&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell, not even the THEOI sealed away all the Titans. Helios? Still unbound. Hecate is arguably Titan<i>ic</i> and she's out and about. And there's mythic sources that imply that Kronos was never bound, and in fact is just chilling on some island minding his own business.<br /> <br /> To be honest I kind of don't like the idea of things gearing up for a Second Titan War, because I think it's a disservice to the Pantheons involved to try and imply it's in any way a unified front. At my table, the Titans are a THREAT, but they're not teaming up in some kind of Greater War. It doesn't make any sense for say, Prometheus and Surtr to team up just because it was decided that all Titans should be grouped by Elements that they may or may not even be that applicable under. (I love 2e but I politely disagree with giving Prometheus the Fire Purview, and bemoan that there's nothing like Awareness as a Purview, as his Titan Thing was Foresight IIRC)<br /> <br /> And at my table, I handwave a rise in Titanspawn sightings and incidents to not being a sign that the Titans are coming back, but to any number of other things. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>There aren't more Titanspawn, humans are just expanding and are encountering them more</li> <li>There aren't more Titanspawn, humanity is just better at recognizing them. Much like how it's not that we suddenly have a rise of people who are on the Autism Spectrum, we just know what that is now and know how to recognize it. (Disclaimer: No I'm not comparing people on the Autism Spectrum to Titanspawn, I'm just using it as an example of how seeing more of something doesn't mean there's suddenly more of it)</li> <li>There are <i>enough</i> cultures that seem to use the idea of Heroic Ages and Cycles. Maybe another is approaching, because That's How It Works.</li> </ol><br /> And I personally note that Titanspawn aren't always directly linked to the Titans. Like, sure, cyclopses may have worked for the Titans, but many also worked for the Gods, and you can't be sure that a cyclops is working for Titans, working for a God, or heck even if they're just working for themselves. Titanspawn is probably a very widely-applied term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:33:02-07:00","id":1391263,"title":"","content":"I am not saying there isn't conflict. the titanspawn are still around, but they have never needed scions until now. <br /> <br /> also I count Apep in the same category as the Fenris Wolf and the World Serpent. This category I call the pantheon busters. <br /> <br /> but I just like the 1st ed portrayal, I love the idea of musphelhiem having Prometheus and stuff. I like how it explains why the tians weren't killed. I just prefer first ed, <br /> <br /> I am not trying to get sucked into a debate about some unresolvable conflict. Had enough of that with the whole council of Nikea/ rune priests are psykers thing over on alternate history.com. But I do want to know why the second titan war has only been recognized now. <br /> <br /> I am willing to accept that the gods are still fighting the titans, but what has changed to nessisate scions. indeed, if what you say is true, and the Aztecs are still fighting hordes of star demons and such. if this has been happening forever why are scions needed now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:54:50-07:00","id":1391268,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think there is a need of Scions in special now, but there is need for a constant flux of new scions to fight a war that is raging for eons. Scions die too often to count them as future gods or even to count on a few of them to save the world, what the gods need are soldiers that can beat the higher level titanspawn while they are fighting the Titans themselves<br /> <br /> At least that my approach on the 1e Metaplot, and what I felt when read thru 1e God fictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:56:45-07:00","id":1391269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391268#post1391268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think there is a need of Scions in special now, but there is need for a constant flux of new scions to fight a war that is raging for eons. Scions die too often to count them as future gods or even to count on a few of them to save the world, what the gods need are soldiers that can beat the higher level titanspawn while themselves are fighting the Titans themselves.<br /> <br /> At least that my approach on the 1e Metaplot, and what I felt when read thru 1e God fictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>that makes sense for 2ed. <br /> <br /> I prefer 1st ed, espically the titans of that ed. if you don't agree, then lets just agree to disagree on that front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:03:45-07:00","id":1391272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391269#post1391269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that makes sense for 2ed.<br /> <br /> I prefer 1st ed, espically the titans of that ed. if you don't agree, then lets just agree to disagree on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the approach they made on 1e, but it is completely Theoi-centric and is far from fitting any other pantheon.<br /> <br /> If I was running a game of Scion, I would focus on a pantheon (Theoi, in my mind) and make it close to 1e metaplot.<br /> <br /> But forcing this approach to the other pantheons (as it sounded on 1e) is not the best way to deal. So I agree with the 2e idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:07:09-07:00","id":1391274,"title":"","content":"You know you don't have to repeat that your prefer 1e with every post right... We've gathered that by now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, your question assumes that Scions are being newly created now... There's no actual reason to assume this... The Pantheons have *always* been making Scions throughout history, you just happen to be playing one in this current age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:11:04-07:00","id":1391277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391274#post1391274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know you don't have to repeat that your prefer 1e with every post right... We've gathered that by now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, your question assumes that Scions are being newly created now... There's no actual reason to assume this... The Pantheons have *always* been making Scions throughout history, you just happen to be playing one in this current age.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, that I have gathered. ok then. <br /> <br /> But if this is true, then why is it only called the second titan war now. if there have always been scions then why is the term second titan war new?<br /> <br /> I am operating under an assumption that it only started being used in the 60s. at least, I think that's what Origins said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:18:33-07:00","id":1391281,"title":"","content":"Firstly, there's a bunch of ideas in the initial setting chapter that get completely ignored in the rest of the book, and for the best, such as the idea of Primordials having World Bodies (which every single Pantheon thankfully ignores)... I would treat the idea of a 'Second' Titan War much like that... Secondly, the idea of even a first unified Titan War is itself ridiculous given that there are Pantheons that don't even acknowledge a difference between Gods and Titans to begin with... Kind of hard to have a War with things you don't believe exist \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> I would ignore the idea of a unified War completely, and focus on more mythically appropriate opposition for the Pantheons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 05-24-2020, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:27:45-07:00","id":1391289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391281#post1391281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, there's a bunch of ideas in the Indian setting chapter that get completely ignored in the rest of the book, and for the best, such as the idea of Primordials having World Bodies (which every single Pantheon thankfully ignores)... I would treat the idea of a 'Second' Titan War much like that... Secondly, the idea of even a first unified Titan War is itself ridiculous given that there are Pantheons that don't even acknowledge a difference between Gods and Titans to begin with... Kind of hard to have a War with things you don't believe exist \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> I would ignore the idea of a unified War completely, and focus on more mythically appropriate opposition for the Pantheons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>um, like what? I don't get what your saying. <br /> <br /> also, as I have repeatedly stated, I love 1st ed, so I like the whole unified war and unified titans. that might not be popular, bur I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:34:23-07:00","id":1391294,"title":"","content":"Oops, autocorrect changed initial to Indian <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am saying that the idea of a Unified Titan War, first or second, makes no sense in keeping with actual mythology... If you want to include them, feel free, but at that point since you're ignoring so much of the mythology of the Pantheons you don't really *need* an official reason for a Second War do you? You can just go with the 1e idea that all Pantheons have Antagonistic Titans and that they were sealed off a long time ago and have started getting out now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:44:42-07:00","id":1391307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391294#post1391294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oops, autocorrect changed initial to Indian <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am saying that the idea of a Unified Titan War, first or second, makes no sense in keeping with actual mythology... If you want to include them, feel free, but at that point since you're ignoring so much of the mythology of the Pantheons you don't really *need* an official reason for a Second War do you? You can just go with the 1e idea that all Pantheons have Antagonistic Titans and that they were sealed off a long time ago and have started getting out now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, honestly i am not running a scion game. I just see the pantheons working together for the titan war and just going there seperate ways except for major things (like ww2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:49:48-07:00","id":1391312,"title":"","content":"Ah, good luck in getting to run/play in one then, assuming you're interested in that aspect of Scion. Either way I hope that answers your question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:59:58-07:00","id":1391317,"title":"","content":"I'm not really planing to run/play scion. But the question still stands, if this is the first time pantheons are united, where does the term second titan war comes from. What changed to make the pantheons need to unite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:03:25-07:00","id":1391320,"title":"","content":"Simple... The Pantheons *aren't* United and there is no second Titan War, because there are quite a few Pantheons that are not at large scale war with their Titans (or even acknowledge having them) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> you can safely ignore that bit of the lore of 2e cuz the rest of the book does... The beginning of the Pantheon chapter in Hero even goes into the details of how the different Pantheons have widely different stances in this issue and aren't United in the least <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:12:21-07:00","id":1391325,"title":"","content":"I think Titanomachy might answer a lot of these questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:13:33-07:00","id":1391326,"title":"","content":"Ok then. Seems like my question has been answered (i kinda stopped careing a while ago)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:30:09-07:00","id":1391336,"title":"","content":"Why u stop caring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:36:55-07:00","id":1391337,"title":"","content":"Ultimately if you prefer 1e's portrayal, that's it, use that, end of conversation.<br /> <br /> I personally don't, because I find that there's nothing it does that's particularly GOOD, and the only thing it does well is homogenize religions and cosmologies that actually aren't really that similar in any way.<br /> <br /> Instead of 2e acknowledging &quot;Hey these religions and myths actually don't map cleanly to a Greek-style relationship of Good Gods Bad Titans maybe we should explore that more as a game opportunity&quot;, 1e went &quot;Yeah but let's just throw all these entities that are kind of similar if you squint and are drunk and don't actually research three quarters of them that well&quot; and lo, suddenly we have Surtr, Prometheus, and Kagutuschi who are figures who have fuck all to do with one another, all working together and said to be aspects of the greater whole because they may or may not have some burny associations.<br /> <br /> (Echoing again how I don't think Prometheus should be a Fire Titan anymore than I don't think Shiva should have Beasts (Cattle) just because he rides a bull)<br /> <br /> But at BEST it's grossly oversimplifying the actual rich history and lore of these figures, and at worst it's getting... Well it's more than a little Campbell. Like, even if Campbell's theories REALLY oversimplified things and drew parallels where there were none, this is if anything even moreso.<br /> <br /> And I don't think even if it were 'neat' (I disagree as I feel that it kind of makes the figures boring by going &quot;Yeah they're basically faces of the same thing&quot;) that it's a good idea to commit to something like that. Like, I'm not going to throw shade at 1e's writers or accuse them of malice when I'm sure they did what they could and wanted to do well but may not have had access to good resources for adequate research... But the actual results are... <i>Not great?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:49:29-07:00","id":1391339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391336#post1391336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why u stop caring?</div> </div> </div> </div>honestly, this turned into a debate about 1ed vs 2ed, I didn't want that. I wanted to see what was earlier in the thread. namely ideas why its eclated enough to become a new titan war. climate change freeing the titans. a godly legion of doom. things like that. now its blathering about mythology concerns. its entertainment, it does not have to be 100 percent accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:55:40-07:00","id":1391342,"title":"","content":"It's entertainment that's dealing with subjects that are extremely important to large sections of often marginalised people, so even if 100% accuracy is not achievable, respect absolutely should be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And 1e has the dubious distinction in that members of two separate extremely heterodox religions (Zoroastrianism and Hinduism) which have next to no concept of heresy or blasphemy, read their portrayals in it and went 'yup... That's blasphemy alright'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:00:14-07:00","id":1391348,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> wow. I didn\u2019t know that. I never read 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:00:18-07:00","id":1391349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391342#post1391342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entertainment that's dealing with subjects that are extremely important to large sections of often marginalised people, so even if 100% accuracy is not achievable, respect absolutely should be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And 1e has the dubious distinction in that members of two separate extremely heterodox religions (Zoroastrianism and Hinduism) which have next to no concept of heresy or blasphemy, read their portrayals in it and went 'yup... That's blasphemy alright'</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that last part hard to believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:18:51-07:00","id":1391355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391349#post1391349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find that last part hard to believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which part? That Zoroastrianism and Hinduism don't really have a concept of blasphemy or that 1e managed it regardless <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?<br /> <br /> I am the Hindu in question, and the Zoroastrian is the writer for the 2e Yazata, but I doubt that will allay your doubts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> suffice to say that the 1e Hindu Pantheon unwittingly parroted right wing nationalist propaganda, decided that one of the strongest Goddesses was being forced to act as a brood mare by her husband against her will, portrayed one of the most widely loved Gods as seducing his students behind his wife's back (both individually blasphemous, they managed to double down on it), and used material from Marvel Comics as part of the Cosmology... I'm sure I'm missing something but to go through the whole chapter would probably break not just the post's character limit but the server's storage limit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:27:55-07:00","id":1391359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391355#post1391355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which part? That Zoroastrianism and Hinduism don't really have a concept of blasphemy or that 1e managed it regardless <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?<br /> <br /> I am the Hindu in question, and the Zoroastrian is the writer for the 2e Yazata, but I doubt that will allay your doubts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> suffice to say that the 1e Hindu Pantheon unwittingly parroted right wing nationalist propaganda, decided that one of the strongest Goddesses was being forced to act as a brood mare by her husband against her will, portrayed one of the most widely loved Gods as seducing his students behind his wife's back (both individually blasphemous, they managed to double down on it), and used material from Marvel Comics as part of the Cosmology... I'm sure I'm missing something but to go through the whole chapter would probably break not just the post's character limit but the server's storage limit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>both. I didn't get any brood mare readings from the hundu pantheon, or any cheating from (I want to say shiva, but I might be wrong). also the only marvel comics reference I know to exist in scion ragnorok where the asier agree to not mess with the thor comics. <br /> <br /> I am in the dark here about all this apparently. how did they manage to do right wing nationalist propaganda. <br /> <br /> I mean, I don't know much about Hinduism or Zoroastrian. the only pantheons I can claim to know are greek, norse and Egyptian. <br /> <br /> I am just confused and half hoping the mods strike down this thread too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:36:25-07:00","id":1391360,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1344_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1344\" data-vbnamecard=\"1344\">Samudra</a> thanks. Like I said, I didn\u2019t know all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:18:59-07:00","id":1391372,"title":"","content":"There is a legend that tells that the first settlement in Rome was funded by Saturn (I dear there are indications that the Capitoline Hill were occupied since the Bronze Age, thousand years before the Oficial Fundation), and the famous columns in the Forums are from the temple of Saturn. That would put the idea of Kronos out of the Tartarus AND helping his children in a time much later to the Titanomachia.<br /> <br /> There is a reason for that, Saturn was father to Jupiter before Jupiter becoming Zeus (what made Saturn Kronos), as Jupiter was Etruscan/Latin god, that was \u201cGreekfied\u201d when the Roman Patricii were Hiring / slaving Greeks to teach philosophy to their kids.<br /> <br /> Yet, it make part (the largest part in absolute numbers) of the worshipers believe in a story that Goes against the most important story of the entire myth (and the exact one that is talked here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:20:35-07:00","id":1391394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391359#post1391359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> both. I didn't get any brood mare readings from the hundu pantheon, or any cheating from (I want to say shiva, but I might be wrong). also the only marvel comics reference I know to exist in scion ragnorok where the asier agree to not mess with the thor comics.<br /> <br /> I am in the dark here about all this apparently. how did they manage to do right wing nationalist propaganda.<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't know much about Hinduism or Zoroastrian. the only pantheons I can claim to know are greek, norse and Egyptian.<br /> <br /> I am just confused and half hoping the mods strike down this thread too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Samudra, but I can make some notes.<br /> <br /> Edit: Note that I'm referring to the write-ups in 1e's Companion book, where it had the Deva of 1e. Nothing I say applies to the 2e writeups of the characters, which are very good. Just thought I'd make it explicit.<br /> <br /> Parvati's write-up mentions that she feels uncomfortable having new Scions (and since this is 1e the only way to have Scions was to have a God fuck a human and very rarely adopt which was mentioned in a sidebar in the Deva writeup so the writer didn't HAVE to go here BUT DID-) but she does so because Shiva makes her. Which is GROSSLY out of character for Shiva (and just plain gross).<br /> <br /> Shiva, meanwhile, is mentioned in his bio in 1e as holding yoga classes and sleeping with his students to father new Scions. Which as Samudra mentions is a twofold Thing Shiva Would Never Do, because one, Shiva would never cheat on his wife and this is basically a cosmic constant, same with all the other Deva... And as he mentioned, teacher-student sexual relationships to the Deva would be basically the One Unforgivable Sin.<br /> <br /> And the reference to Marvel Comics in the Scion Companion is that it mentions Kali as being Shiva's daughter. She's not. In some branches of Hinduism, she's (one of) his wives, but in NO school of Hinduism is she his daughter. She IS, however, his daughter in the Marvel Continuities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-24-2020, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:54:57-07:00","id":1391403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391394#post1391394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not Samudra, but I can make some notes.<br /> <br /> Edit: Note that I'm referring to the write-ups in 1e's Companion book, where it had the Deva of 1e. Nothing I say applies to the 2e writeups of the characters, which are very good. Just thought I'd make it explicit.<br /> <br /> Parvati's write-up mentions that she feels uncomfortable having new Scions (and since this is 1e the only way to have Scions was to have a God fuck a human and very rarely adopt which was mentioned in a sidebar in the Deva writeup so the writer didn't HAVE to go here BUT DID-) but she does so because Shiva makes her. Which is GROSSLY out of character for Shiva (and just plain gross).<br /> <br /> Shiva, meanwhile, is mentioned in his bio in 1e as holding yoga classes and sleeping with his students to father new Scions. Which as Samudra mentions is a twofold Thing Shiva Would Never Do, because one, Shiva would never cheat on his wife and this is basically a cosmic constant, same with all the other Deva... And as he mentioned, teacher-student sexual relationships to the Deva would be basically the One Unforgivable Sin.<br /> <br /> And the reference to Marvel Comics in the Scion Companion is that it mentions Kali as being Shiva's daughter. She's not. In some branches of Hinduism, she's (one of) his wives, but in NO school of Hinduism is she his daughter. She IS, however, his daughter in the Marvel Continuities.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok then. I didn't know those two things. I honestly didn't know shiva was teaching yoga classes, and cheating on his wife. also, I never assumed kali was shiva's daughter. his wife yes, but not daughter. from the (admittedly uninformed) opion of this poster, shiva is only doing this because the titans are loose and they need all the help they can get. <br /> <br /> please dont flame me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T20:01:38-07:00","id":1391406,"title":"","content":"No one is flaming you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T20:11:14-07:00","id":1391409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391406#post1391406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is flaming you.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, it sure feels like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:04:32-07:00","id":1391413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391409#post1391409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> well, it sure feels like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I was just noting some Problems that I personally have with the 1e writeups now that I've been told about them from someone who's in a position to know (I had these pointed out to me by Samudra). Like, until I had someone go &quot;Yo this isn't cool because X Y and Z&quot; my only takeaway from 1e's Deva writeup was &quot;Wow these Gods sound kinda boring&quot; which while a shame since the Deva are emphatically NOT boring it wasn't the worst thing written in there.<br /> <br /> Not knowing isn't something that should be punished. REFUSING TO LEARN, maybe, but honestly? You probably didn't know how many liberties 1e took with the source material, often ones that were kind of offensive or at the very least Very Not Cool.<br /> <br /> And I haven't been aiming anything at you, at least not intentionally. I have no idea who you are, I don't have an opinion of you. I have Opinions on some of the things in 1e but that's not related. I've tried to keep my posts focused on that. &quot;This is how I run things-&quot; &quot;I personally prefer this&quot; and &quot;I didn't like this part of 1e because of these reasons&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:25:54-07:00","id":1391422,"title":"","content":"I did not know the liberties taken. The fact that its portrayal can be considered blashemy in religeons that have little to no concept of blasphemy shocks me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:26:40-07:00","id":1391423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391409#post1391409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> well, it sure feels like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s definitely not about flaming you. This subject come more than once in the last few years, and every time there are some discussion about how 1e describe the gods out of their religion and how second edition did a better job by just not forcing any metaplot at all.<br /> <br /> Many people here is pacionate for the subject before even the books existed, and so they let their passion flame the discussion a bit more than usual for RPG forums. Also, for some it\u2019s about their religions, so it\u2019s quite serious and personal.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t be offended, and, as Kyman201 signature says, if you are having fun you are not doing wrong, just not expect everybody to agree with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T04:07:16-07:00","id":1391454,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26173\" data-vbnamecard=\"26173\">evtrax</a> you\u2019re good. People just get passionate sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T06:26:23-07:00","id":1391467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391454#post1391454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> you\u2019re good. People just get passionate sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Ok then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T16:52:32-07:00","id":1391567,"title":"","content":"I'm synthesizing stuff from both editions together, personally. I, much like you, like a full-scale divine conflict to provide a backdrop, but I much prefer the depictions of both the titans and the gods in 2e.<br /> <br /> My work around is that the conflict isn't ALL titans vs. ALL gods, but there is a large scale war erupting, with a single Big Bad having rallied a bunch of the more destructive/sinister titans, monsters, and renegade gods from multiple mythologies under his banner, to try and impose a new cosmic hierarchy on the World. This attempt at totalitarian cosmic conquest is what has brought the pantheons together, including any titanic allies they maintain good relations with. I haven't figured out who I want as that Big Bad though.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I liked the 1e element of there being a &quot;masquerade&quot; of sorts, but was kind of irritated at the lack of any real mechanic to maintain it, so I currently have a vague, handwave-y &quot;Mists of Fate&quot; that kind obscures divine action from the masses, but the more mythical stuff that happens in an area at once, the thinner the Mists get, and a person exposed multiple times starts to see through the mist by default, and becomes vulnerable to fatebinding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T18:51:38-07:00","id":1391582,"title":"","content":"I like the magical realism (?) atmosphere of Scion 2e. It\u2019s a refreshing change from the Masquerade emphasis in WoD and CoD.<br /> <br /> For the record, I totally agree that Parvati being raped by her husband and Shiva doing stuff with his students is gross, but I never actually read Scion 1e, plus I figured pretty much everyone on the forums agrees that\u2019s pretty bad, so I didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> Question: is Scion Ragnar\u00f6k worth reading? (Oh wow. My autocorrect put those two little dots over the o in Ragnar\u00f6k.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T19:47:57-07:00","id":1391597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391582#post1391582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the magical realism (?) atmosphere of Scion 2e. It\u2019s a refreshing change from the Masquerade emphasis in WoD and CoD.<br /> <br /> For the record, I totally agree that Parvati being raped by her husband and Shiva doing stuff with his students is gross, but I never actually read Scion 1e, plus I figured pretty much everyone on the forums agrees that\u2019s pretty bad, so I didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> Question: is Scion Ragnar\u00f6k worth reading? (Oh wow. My autocorrect put those two little dots over the o in Ragnar\u00f6k.)</div> </div> </div> </div>on ragnorok, yes! I really like it, but then again I love 1st ed. I love the mythological adventure it provides. If you want me to tell you the two big twists I will, but if you don't want spoiliers I will still my tounge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:30:50-07:00","id":1391605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391582#post1391582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: is Scion Ragnar\u00f6k worth reading? (Oh wow. My autocorrect put those two little dots over the o in Ragnar\u00f6k.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ragnarok is an interesting book? Like, I highly suggest people read it to get an understanding of how the Developers of 1e imagined full Legend 1 - 12 Campaigns to go. What I find so interesting about it is that the... the image the Devs had of how a game of Scion would 'work' was totally different than every campaign and game of 1e I ever ran or played in, and I played once or twice a week for six years.<br /> <br /> It has some... fictional elements, but thankfully nothing as flat out offensive as seen in other books. IIRC they actually fuck up the order of events of Ragnarok which helps throw off your players, but also... I mean that's not how Wyrd works? The order of events of Ragnarok are being enforced with the same force of the actual conclusions. There is also a <i>really</i> interesting focus the writers had on trying to make the events of Ragnarok semi-scientific which is interesting, again, from a like... designer perspective of how people would play their game. <br /> <br /> Oh! There's this weird thing where Hel becomes beautiful with Baldur showing up which is like... that's got some implications. And the writers really cast Nana in a <i>super</i> negative light.<br /> <br /> If you aren't interested in the history and developmental growth of Scion, I would say it is a sort of 'meh' read? But, like, if you are interested in the weird and finicky and development and growth of Scion, totally check it out. Just, bring a critical eye to it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:40:44-07:00","id":1391607,"title":"","content":"Thank you \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26173\" data-vbnamecard=\"26173\">evtrax</a> let\u2019s hold off on the spoilers \ud83d\ude0a. I\u2019m probably gonna get Ragnar\u00f6k. I like Norse stuff, and I\u2019m kinda bored this week, so I\u2019ll probably end up reading it and let you know what I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T03:20:36-07:00","id":1391656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391605#post1391605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ragnarok is an interesting book? Like, I highly suggest people read it to get an understanding of how the Developers of 1e imagined full Legend 1 - 12 Campaigns to go. What I find so interesting about it is that the... the image the Devs had of how a game of Scion would 'work' was totally different than every campaign and game of 1e I ever ran or played in, and I played once or twice a week for six years.<br /> <br /> It has some... fictional elements, but thankfully nothing as flat out offensive as seen in other books. IIRC they actually fuck up the order of events of Ragnarok which helps throw off your players, but also... I mean that's not how Wyrd works? The order of events of Ragnarok are being enforced with the same force of the actual conclusions. There is also a <i>really</i> interesting focus the writers had on trying to make the events of Ragnarok semi-scientific which is interesting, again, from a like... designer perspective of how people would play their game. <br /> <br /> Oh! There's this weird thing where Hel becomes beautiful with Baldur showing up which is like... that's got some implications. And the writers really cast Nana in a <i>super</i> negative light.<br /> <br /> If you aren't interested in the history and developmental growth of Scion, I would say it is a sort of 'meh' read? But, like, if you are interested in the weird and finicky and development and growth of Scion, totally check it out. Just, bring a critical eye to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friends and I got Ragnarok and I decided to run the campaign setting almost beat for beat. I mean, I tweaked the story here and there. I added some new stuff along the way. But the campaign was pretty much the spine of the entire game.<br /> <br /> It's not a coincidence that my friends still say that that was our best campaign ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T04:00:15-07:00","id":1391665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391567#post1391567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm synthesizing stuff from both editions together, personally. I, much like you, like a full-scale divine conflict to provide a backdrop, but I much prefer the depictions of both the titans and the gods in 2e.<br /> <br /> My work around is that the conflict isn't ALL titans vs. ALL gods, but there is a large scale war erupting, with a single Big Bad having rallied a bunch of the more destructive/sinister titans, monsters, and renegade gods from multiple mythologies under his banner, to try and impose a new cosmic hierarchy on the World. This attempt at totalitarian cosmic conquest is what has brought the pantheons together, including any titanic allies they maintain good relations with. I haven't figured out who I want as that Big Bad though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This is what I would be going for with my concept of a Titanomachy, and what I suspect the writers have in mind with the Titanomachy book. Such a scenario would provide boundless opportunities to have figures from multiple pantheons interact, which is a major draw of Scion for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T08:01:10-07:00","id":1391679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391567#post1391567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm synthesizing stuff from both editions together, personally. I, much like you, like a full-scale divine conflict to provide a backdrop, but I much prefer the depictions of both the titans and the gods in 2e.<br /> <br /> My work around is that the conflict isn't ALL titans vs. ALL gods, but there is a large scale war erupting, with a single Big Bad having rallied a bunch of the more destructive/sinister titans, monsters, and renegade gods from multiple mythologies under his banner, to try and impose a new cosmic hierarchy on the World. This attempt at totalitarian cosmic conquest is what has brought the pantheons together, including any titanic allies they maintain good relations with. I haven't figured out who I want as that Big Bad though.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I liked the 1e element of there being a &amp;quot;masquerade&amp;quot; of sorts, but was kind of irritated at the lack of any real mechanic to maintain it, so I currently have a vague, handwave-y &amp;quot;Mists of Fate&amp;quot; that kind obscures divine action from the masses, but the more mythical stuff that happens in an area at once, the thinner the Mists get, and a person exposed multiple times starts to see through the mist by default, and becomes vulnerable to fatebinding.</div> </div> </div> </div>When in doubt, use loki.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T08:38:45-07:00","id":1391683,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"679\" data-vbnamecard=\"679\">unnatural1</a> that\u2019s really cool. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T13:21:23-07:00","id":1391766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391679#post1391679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When in doubt, use loki.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I thought about it, but I feel more sympathetic to Loki, who wasn't quite the &quot;almost satan&quot; they're viewed as in popular culture. If anything, I might use Typhon, a reincarnation of Ravana, or Ahriman as my big bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T13:50:06-07:00","id":1391771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zealot_Vedas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391766#post1391766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I thought about it, but I feel more sympathetic to Loki, who wasn't quite the &quot;almost satan&quot; they're viewed as in popular culture. If anything, I might use Typhon, a reincarnation of Ravana, or Ahriman as my big bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm. ok then. those are all good choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T14:29:47-07:00","id":1391777,"title":"","content":"Figures I'm considering for my legions of doom include Angra Mainyu (the one who brings them all together), Ravana, Balor, Yeluri, Asuang, Surtr, Tawiscara, Coyolxauhqui, Erlik Khan, maybe Chiyou, maybe Supay, Tau, Aten (as the Starscream type), Ushuni (who goes off on his own and is ultimately too hard too control), Eris (only in it for the shits and giggles), at least one of the Lakota titans, maybe Yum Cimil, and Yayael. Also a lot of lesser Titans who serve those ones, like Zahhak, Bres, etc. They also end up unleashing Typhon as their nuclear option, but keep him on a tight leash. I think it would be more or less in character, mythologically speaking, for most of them. If you know more than I do in that regard, then by all means, correct me. I'm trying to select figures who are A. sapient and rational enough to form alliances of convenience, B. not gods who are evil but still loyal members of their pantheons, and C. legitimately malicious and tyrannical, not merely &quot;complex.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 05-26-2020, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T14:43:57-07:00","id":1391779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391777#post1391777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Figures I'm considering for my legions of doom include Angra Mainyu (the one who brings them all together), Ravana, Balor, Yeluri, Asuang, Surtr, Tawiscara, Coyolxauhqui, Erlik Khan, maybe Chiyou, Aten (as the Starscream type), Ushuni (who goes off on his own and is ultimately too hard too control), Eris (only in it for the shits and giggles), at least one of the Lakota titans, maybe Yum Cimil, and Yayael. Also a lot of lesser Titans who serve those ones, like Zahhak, Bres, etc. They also end up unleashing Typhon as their nuclear option, but keep him on a tight leash. I think it would be more or less in character, mythologically speaking, for most of them. If you know more than I do in that regard, than by all means, correct me.</div> </div> </div> </div>aten as starscream, hard yes. He was always my least favorite titan. Or more accurately the one I loved to hate. some of my christan faith might get offended. but its all for fun. <br /> <br /> I also like typhon being there last resort. I will need to look up a few names of your legion, but you've got a great roster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T14:54:20-07:00","id":1391783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391777#post1391777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-<br /> They also end up unleashing Typhon as their nuclear option, but keep him on a tight leash.<br /> -snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd have to, given that he was created with the express purpose of both defeating Zeus and replacing him as the new king of the cosmos, and very nearly succeeded. He could very easily wind up taking over the &quot;Legion of Doom&quot; if given half a chance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T15:10:19-07:00","id":1391786,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the way they handle Typhon might be through Echidna, who seems to be more reasonable and the only one who might be capable of convincing Typhon to do things for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T16:57:58-07:00","id":1391807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1391786#post1391786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that the way they handle Typhon might be through Echidna, who seems to be more reasonable and the only one who might be capable of convincing Typhon to do things for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>echidna is his wife. or his mother. I forget which, but she has a better chance at controlling the being whose so angry they had to add a vent to his prison than most beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T17:17:30-07:00","id":1391812,"title":"","content":"Echidna is his wife. Gaea is his mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"