br /> <br /> There they are! The LOD, as I'm envisioning them! If anyone has any reason why these any of these guys wouldn't work, please tell me.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>The Divine Legion of Doom in all its horrible glory. its perfect!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T20:39:28-07:00","id":1392116,"title":"","content":"Honestly Aten is... how can I say... not evil? He is evil from the point of view of the Netjer, because they where put aside by the Pharaoh, not different from the Jeova from the point of view of the Theoi in Rome or TDD in Ireland, or the Manitou in US or Teotl in Mexico, or... well all the other pantheons that were abandoned for a Monotheist belief. The only difference is that the polytheist priests defeated the monotheist Pharaoh and returned to the Polytheistic belief system.<br /> <br /> Apep (Apophis) is by far a better enemy of the Netjer, they actually fight EVERY SINGLE NIGHT!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-27-2020, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:26:12-07:00","id":1392219,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz totally agree!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:16:56-07:00","id":1392234,"title":"","content":"I mean maybe I'm the odd one but I don't really think that the Titans need to band together in any kind of large capacity. Most of them have their own agendas and desires, and not all of them have a lot of overlap. Like I don't think Apep has a very big interest in working together, since his motivations begin and end with &quot;Eat Ra, end everything&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell I saw someone joke that even in cases where their aims kinda overlap (like various Entities that want to eat the sun) you can actually use that as a way to divide them by going &quot;So hey, Fenrir, if Apep eats the sun what're you going to do come Ragnarok?&quot; and then the fight starts.<br /> <br /> I dunno, going full &quot;Titan Legion of Doom&quot; feels like it's doing stuff that doesn't make a lot of sense to me and when you think about it doesn't really ADD anything to the story that's needed. Will your players really NEED to know that Angra Mainyu signed off on Apep's plan to Keep Doing What He Does? Like, most of these Baddies have been doing what they do for a LONG time, following their own aims.<br /> <br /> And most of them have coexisted for a very long time as well. So why are they only NOW going &quot;What if we team up?&quot; Like I can see rare instances where some of them may work together, but often a lot of them have such DIFFERENT goals that I can't see many of them working together. Why would Bres the Bright, the Fomorian King, want to sign on with the Titans who want to end everything when Bres, most likely, would want Ireland again?<br /> <br /> To say nothing of competing timetables. Will Surtr actually be interested in helping someone else burn the world down when that's HIS job, and he knows it's going to happen come Ragnarok? Surtr knows what's going to happen and he's probably VERY eager for it.<br /> <br /> I dunno, it feels like the more Titanic figures you try to add and try to claim &quot;No they're all working together&quot; the less sense it makes. That's why I tend to go with &quot;Sometimes these divine figures may work together for a short time but most of them are content doing their own thing&quot;<br /> <br /> Not that I'm against crossovers. One of my Plot Ideas is the idea that Kali and Shiva have incarnated and are currently at a night club, tearing up the dance floor (literally), with a last-minute complication of Eris rolling a golden apple between the two of them that says <i>To The One With The Best Moves</i>. But that's not because Ravana or another Asura bribed Eris, that was just that Eris saw an opportunity to make things Silly and took it. Does it need to be more than that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:27:41-07:00","id":1392238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1392116#post1392116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly Aten is... how can I say... not evil? He is evil from the point of view of the Netjer, because they where put aside by the Pharaoh, not different from the Jeova from the point of view of the Theoi in Rome or TDD in Ireland, or the Manitou in US or Teotl in Mexico, or... well all the other pantheons that were abandoned for a Monotheist belief. The only difference is that the polytheist priests defeated the monotheist Pharaoh and returned to the Polytheistic belief system.<br /> <br /> Apep (Apophis) is by far a better enemy of the Netjer, they actually fight EVERY SINGLE NIGHT!</div> </div> </div> </div>The aten of 1e is evil. A solphist of pure might who strips the will of all his servants. I can totally see that aten pulling a starscream. Maybe mythological aten isnt evil, but i only know of his scion counterpart.<br /> <br /> Wrote this on my phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T11:07:50-07:00","id":1392261,"title":"","content":"I feel like that's largely a matter of personal taste. My response to that is, no, it doesn't have to be any more than that, but it would be insanely cool if it was. My tastes in fiction in general are, admittedly, very comic book-y. To me, a massive divine war that includes a ton of different pantheons would be the coolest thing imaginable. As long as my depictions of all the figures involved are reasonably in character, and not offensive to their cultures of origin, I feel like it can be workable, albeit requiring a lot of careful thought and research to pull off. As for timetables and the individual motivations of each Titan for joining the group, that, obviously will require justifications and while I don't necessarily have all of them yet, I don't think it's an unsurmountable problem. Also, I will say that this roster was very much off the top of my head and not final. I'm strongly considering dropping Surtr and just having Utgard-Loki instead, as you make a very good point that Surtr is more about pure devastation and ending the world than conquering it, so he might be directly at odds with the rest of them, as I imagine this group as being primarily conquest driven with a few select members who joined because they want vengeance against the gods or are simply in it &quot;for the evulz.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for Apep, that's exactly the reason why I didn't include him to begin with and went with Aten instead. Apep is an all-consuming monstrosity who I suspect Angra Mainyu and the others would have viewed as completely uncontrollable, and whose goals would be opposed to their conquest-based ones. As for Aten, on the other hand, the way I envision him is more of a schemer. Admittedly, my reason for putting him on the list is more due to the meta-narrative than the events of the myths themselves. It's basically the result of me imagining what would have gone on among the Netjer themselves while his cult achieved temporary dominance in Egypt. And I'm imagining a scenario where he tried to take over the pantheon by force and establish himself as Egypt's only god. The reason this isn't recorded in the mythology is, very simply, that the Netjer are embarrassed. They don't want to admit that one god almost managed to destroy and/or banish all of the rest of them. Now, one thing I will not be doing is what 1e did in regards to conflating Aten with Yahweh and having the Abrahamic religions really be Titanic cults. Both because that's obviously problematic, and because the Malakhim are active players in my world. This is, admittedly, a liberty I'm taking with the myth, but I'm more comfortable doing this with Aten then I would be with a lot of other deities because of the lack of a &quot;canon&quot; characterization that I could find for him, and because I've never actually heard of anyone in modern times who revere him and would be hurt by my depiction. I know him primarily as a historical curiosity, and my understanding is that the Egyptian people at the time (mostly) weren't too fond of him and went back to worshipping the Netjer at the first chance they could.<br /> <br /> My overall premise for this group is pretty similar in a lot of ways to the 2e version of the Keepers of the World. However, while the Keepers are mostly doing it for what they see as the greater good, and are a far smaller, more secretive, group than the &quot;Legion&quot; are, the &quot;Legion&quot; are far more in your face and direct while having no pretentions of benevolence and rely far more on force than on manipulation. The two factions, in my mind, would make great foils for each other, and I'd love to have them interact within the campaign in some way.<br /> <br /> Also, the scenario with Eris, Shiva, and Kali is great and I would love to see that happen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 05-28-2020, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T17:36:16-07:00","id":1392366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1392261#post1392261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like that's largely a matter of personal taste. My response to that is, no, it doesn't have to be any more than that, but it would be insanely cool if it was. My tastes in fiction in general are, admittedly, very comic book-y. To me, a massive divine war that includes a ton of different pantheons would be the coolest thing imaginable. As long as my depictions of all the figures involved are reasonably in character, and not offensive to their cultures of origin, I feel like it can be workable, albeit requiring a lot of careful thought and research to pull off. As for timetables and the individual motivations of each Titan for joining the group, that, obviously will require justifications and while I don't necessarily have all of them yet, I don't think it's an unsurmountable problem. Also, I will say that this roster was very much off the top of my head and not final. I'm strongly considering dropping Surtr and just having Utgard-Loki instead, as you make a very good point that Surtr is more about pure devastation and ending the world than conquering it, so he might be directly at odds with the rest of them, as I imagine this group as being primarily conquest driven with a few select members who joined because they want vengeance against the gods or are simply in it &quot;for the evulz.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for Apep, that's exactly the reason why I didn't include him to begin with and went with Aten instead. Apep is an all-consuming monstrosity who I suspect Angra Mainyu and the others would have viewed as completely uncontrollable, and whose goals would be opposed to their conquest-based ones. As for Aten, on the other hand, the way I envision him is more of a schemer. Admittedly, my reason for putting him on the list is more due to the meta-narrative than the events of the myths themselves. It's basically the result of me imagining what would have gone on among the Netjer themselves while his cult achieved temporary dominance in Egypt. And I'm imagining a scenario where he tried to take over the pantheon by force and establish himself as Egypt's only god. The reason this isn't recorded in the mythology is, very simply, that the Netjer are embarrassed. They don't want to admit that one god almost managed to destroy and/or banish all of the rest of them. Now, one thing I will not be doing is what 1e did in regards to conflating Aten with Yahweh and having the Abrahamic religions really be Titanic cults. Both because that's obviously problematic, and because the Malakhim are active players in my world. This is, admittedly, a liberty I'm taking with the myth, but I'm more comfortable doing this with Aten then I would be with a lot of other deities because of the lack of a &quot;canon&quot; characterization that I could find for him, and because I've never actually heard of anyone in modern times who revere him and would be hurt by my depiction. I know him primarily as a historical curiosity, and my understanding is that the Egyptian people at the time (mostly) weren't too fond of him and went back to worshipping the Netjer at the first chance they could.<br /> <br /> My overall premise for this group is pretty similar in a lot of ways to the 2e version of the Keepers of the World. However, while the Keepers are mostly doing it for what they see as the greater good, and are a far smaller, more secretive, group than the &quot;Legion&quot; are, the &quot;Legion&quot; are far more in your face and direct while having no pretentions of benevolence and rely far more on force than on manipulation. The two factions, in my mind, would make great foils for each other, and I'd love to have them interact within the campaign in some way.<br /> <br /> Also, the scenario with Eris, Shiva, and Kali is great and I would love to see that happen!</div> </div> </div> </div>apep wants to kill everything. the divine legion of doom (that name I gave it just suck in my mind) wants to rule everything. the two goals are mutually exclusive. as for the keepers, they have a benevolent goal, even if one of them is a traitor. <br /> <br /> also, I never saw the 1e aten as being the real church's god. he's just a hoped up arrogant titan whose trying to make himself seem bigger than he really is. if I thought otherwise, I would call blasphemy. but its just a game. and again, aten is the perfect starscream in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T19:27:56-07:00","id":1392390,"title":"","content":"The problem with Aten getting along other Titans is Aten is Monotheistic by definition, and so he would not deal with those \u201cfalse gods\u201d. He killed or absorbed all the other Avatars just because he is the only one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T20:18:21-07:00","id":1392403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1392390#post1392390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Aten getting along other Titans is Aten is Monotheistic by definition, and so he would not deal with those \u201cfalse gods\u201d. He killed or absorbed all the other Avatars just because he is the only one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're talking about two different versions of Aten here. 1e's version of Aten absorbed the other Avatars, but I'm basing mine on the 2e version, which was mentioned in the core book basically as I described him. A megalomaniac god who tried to become the only deity worshipped in his region. My idea for him, within the context of the &quot;Legion&quot; is that he was cast out of the Netjer and/or locked away, but Angra Mainyu ultimately ended up recruiting the disgraced deity as essentially his propagandist, as he was very good at manipulating powerful mortals in order to spread his message. Aten's ambitions have now increased, as, rather than being the monotheistic ruler of one region, he believes that the &quot;Legion&quot; can get rid of all the pantheons for him, and then, if he can somehow find a way to get rid of the rest of the Legion afterwards, he can set himself up as the one god of all of humanity. Angra Mainyu is well aware that he plans to betray them, but is keeping him around for the time being due to his current usefulness. When he outlives said usefulness, however... (makes finger across throat gesture). Basically, it's the classic Starscream/Megatron dynamic with Aten and Angra Mainyu. Aten is behaving as sycophantically as possible towards him, but isn't doing as good a job as he thinks he is in hiding his motivations. Both of them think they're fooling the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 05-28-2020, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T21:13:04-07:00","id":1392747,"title":"","content":"Ragnar\u00f6k is great! It\u2019s a really good campaign that takes your PCs from Hero to God and it\u2019s perfect for an all-Norse band. I especially liked the Demigod arc involving a love quadrangle with the Bright God Baldur, his blind brother Hod, his girlfriend the moon goddess Nanna and the death goddess Hel (Nanna and Hel both love Baldur, Hod loves Nanna and Baldur loves Nanna but kinda likes Hel too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T08:21:03-07:00","id":1392811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1392747#post1392747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ragnar\u00f6k is great! It\u2019s a really good campaign that takes your PCs from Hero to God and it\u2019s perfect for an all-Norse band. I especially liked the Demigod arc involving a love quadrangle with the Bright God Baldur, his blind brother Hod, his girlfriend the moon goddess Nanna and the death goddess Hel (Nanna and Hel both love Baldur, Hod loves Nanna and Baldur loves Nanna but kinda likes Hel too).</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally love that its odin who becomes the big bad trying to avoid his fate. And loki is the one who plays his role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:36:38-07:00","id":1392859,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26173\" data-vbnamecard=\"26173\">evtrax</a> totally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T14:14:22-07:00","id":1392897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1392859#post1392859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26173\" data-vbnamecard=\"26173\">evtrax</a> totally</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like Fenris's redemption. if I played it, I honestly see my character saying, &quot;I don't know. I didn't think we'd get this far.&quot; in response to Fenris asking what they offer in exchange for him staying neutral. <br /> <br /> I also like both versions of nanna's betrayal. I like loki yelling &quot;It wasn't me!&quot;. if I played, I would honestly have my character say, &quot;Its time to cry lady!&quot; to Thokk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T14:38:06-07:00","id":1392902,"title":"","content":"I admit I did like the snark in some of Ragnarok's Sidebars.<br /> <br /> Chiefly, the one that notes &quot;Hey your players may say that Fenris can't run at Ragnarok if they kill him. <b>GEE NONE OF THE OTHER GODS WITH EPIC INTELLIGENCE EVER CONSIDERED THAT!</b> Yes this is a bad idea: Let your players discover that for themselves.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T17:50:26-07:00","id":1392956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1392902#post1392902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I did like the snark in some of Ragnarok's Sidebars.<br /> <br /> Chiefly, the one that notes &quot;Hey your players may say that Fenris can't run at Ragnarok if they kill him. <b>GEE NONE OF THE OTHER GODS WITH EPIC INTELLIGENCE EVER CONSIDERED THAT!</b> Yes this is a bad idea: Let your players discover that for themselves.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah. I also like the visuals in my mind of what they described happening if they managed to kill Fenris. You know, his body becoming a horde of Fenrir, each equal to Garm (the strongest Fenrir in existance) and how they recombind in the final battle to remake Fenris.<br /> <br /> also the fact that if you redeem Fenris his two sons, you know the ones who eat the sun and moon, take there fathers place as the killer of Odin (or rather his body). Also, I might be wrong but I am pretty sure that Fenris kills tyr in the original myth. I like that if you manage to redeem Fenris its Garm who kills Tyr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","user":"evtrax","date":". 05-30-2020, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T18:30:03-07:00","id":1392966,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26173\" data-vbnamecard=\"26173\">evtrax</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> I like how the game makes the victory condition redeeming Fenris instead of actually killing him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T18:59:56-07:00","id":1392971,"title":"","content":"I concur about Fenris having a redemption arc being a great idea. I always saw him as a tragic monster, and a perfect example of the themes of self-fulfilling prophecy that are so prominent in Norse myth. Glad to hear that the big pupper makes it out alive, at least if the game goes positively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T05:17:56-07:00","id":1393060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1392971#post1392971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I concur about Fenris having a redemption arc being a great idea. I always saw him as a tragic monster, and a perfect example of the themes of self-fulfilling prophecy that are so prominent in Norse myth. Glad to hear that the big pupper makes it out alive, at least if the game goes positively.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah. the last challenge you have in his redemption pulled at my heart strings. I put it in the armor pirecing question category of tropes. he asked why tyr, the only god he trusted, who lied and betrayed him, got to be the god of justice. Again, I don't play, but if I did I would have my character give a great speech about how the world isn't fair. about how bad things can be rewarded while the righteous are punished. He would basically say that he doesn't know but that Fenris has been vindicated, and his fate has been defied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:45:36-07:00","id":1393091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1393060#post1393060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah. the last challenge you have in his redemption pulled at my heart strings. I put it in the armor pirecing question category of tropes. he asked why tyr, the only god he trusted, who lied and betrayed him, got to be the god of justice. Again, I don't play, but if I did I would have my character give a great speech about how the world isn't fair. about how bad things can be rewarded while the righteous are punished. He would basically say that he doesn't know but that Fenris has been vindicated, and his fate has been defied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another good answer would be to remind Fenris that Tyr was, ultimately, just. He could've pulled his hand out of Fenris' mouth, but he didn't. He put his hand in his mouth and said &quot;If this is a trick, take my hand.&quot; He allowed his hand to be taken. He didn't really break the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T10:40:22-07:00","id":1393137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1393091#post1393091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another good answer would be to remind Fenris that Tyr was, ultimately, just. He could've pulled his hand out of Fenris' mouth, but he didn't. He put his hand in his mouth and said &amp;quot;If this is a trick, take my hand.&amp;quot; He allowed his hand to be taken. He didn't really break the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. But he still betrayed fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T06:29:32-07:00","id":1393407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1393137#post1393137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes. But he still betrayed fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, undeniably. But Fenris' question was about Tyr's qualification for the job of God of Justice. Not God of Honesty or God of Loyalty. <br /> <br /> He offered recompense if his actions turned out to be deceptive. He delivered that recompense. His actions weren't nice, but they were just.<br /> <br /> It's a subtle distinction, obviously. But it exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T09:03:27-07:00","id":1393445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1393407#post1393407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, undeniably. But Fenris' question was about Tyr's qualification for the job of God of Justice. Not God of Honesty or God of Loyalty.<br /> <br /> He offered recompense if his actions turned out to be deceptive. He delivered that recompense. His actions weren't nice, but they were just.<br /> <br /> It's a subtle distinction, obviously. But it exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, yeah. he did offer his hand. but still, the concept of justice is kinda tied to concepts like honesty and loyalty. Fenris was right to feel betrayed. he was tricked by the only guy he trusted, who wouldn't be angry at that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T10:53:04-07:00","id":1393468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1393445#post1393445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> oh, yeah. he did offer his hand. but still, the concept of justice is kinda tied to concepts like honesty and loyalty. Fenris was right to feel betrayed. he was tricked by the only guy he trusted, who wouldn't be angry at that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course he'd be angry. As you say, who wouldn't? But Tyr was honest as far as Justice went. He made Fenris a promise and he kept it. <br /> <br /> Doesn't mean Fenris doesn't have a right to feel betrayed or angry, but that doesn't disqualify Tyr from being the God of Justice. He did betray Fenris, but then he made some degree of recompense. That's what Justice really focuses on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:05:35-07:00","id":1393497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1393468#post1393468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course he'd be angry. As you say, who wouldn't? But Tyr was honest as far as Justice went. He made Fenris a promise and he kept it.<br /> <br /> Doesn't mean Fenris doesn't have a right to feel betrayed or angry, but that doesn't disqualify Tyr from being the God of Justice. He did betray Fenris, but then he made some degree of recompense. That's what Justice really focuses on.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm. you are right. I have no argument now that you explained it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T10:49:17-07:00","id":1393673,"title":"","content":"There is (probable) cover of <b>Titanomachy</b> book - seems to pointing cross-Pantheons alliances of Titans. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/ShenFei_Titanomachy1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/ShenFei_Titanomachy1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-02-2020, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T11:21:19-07:00","id":1393678,"title":"","content":"I dunno if I'd say that's indicative of anything other than &quot;Lookit these critters&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T13:27:02-07:00","id":1393691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1393673#post1393673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is (probable) cover of <b>Titanomachy</b> book - seems to pointing cross-Pantheons alliances of Titans. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/ShenFei_Titanomachy1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/ShenFei_Titanomachy1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I get just one thing from this: Cool! <br /> <br /> again, I am looking forward to more 2ed. I might prefer the first edition, but I wont turn down any scion product. well, maybe some, but this seems like actual lore rather than a collection of trophies and moves and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T03:58:25-07:00","id":1394747,"title":"","content":"Titans weren't really supposed to be inherently malicious to begin with. Malice is a human concept, and humanity is applied to the Gods.<br /> <br /> Titans are the living embodiment of their purviews. If a fire burns down half a city, it's not because the fire actively wanted to destroy the city. It is the nature of fire to burn all that it comes into contact with. The city just got caught up in the blaze.<br /> <br /> Also, bare in mind that one of the Titans was Gaia, who is supposed to be the spirit of the entire planet. So great, that means 1st edition Scions were technically at war with the earth itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T06:18:03-07:00","id":1394765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewNyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1394747#post1394747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, bare in mind that one of the Titans was Gaia, who is supposed to be the spirit of the entire planet. So great, that means 1st edition Scions were technically at war with the earth itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you mentioning it - with Climate Change / Catastrophy, maybe the ancient sleeping Gaia Titan is waking up -&gt; instant Titan War ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T07:59:07-07:00","id":1394770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1394765#post1394765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you mentioning it - with Climate Change / Catastrophy, maybe the ancient sleeping Gaia Titan is waking up -&gt; instant Titan War ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That actually was one of the theories. See page 1 of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:21:05-07:00","id":1394773,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26211\" data-vbnamecard=\"26211\">NewNyrufa</a> I thought Gaia was supposed to be a Primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:25:35-07:00","id":1394774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1394773#post1394773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26211\" data-vbnamecard=\"26211\">NewNyrufa</a> I thought Gaia was supposed to be a Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She might be in second edition. But in 1st, she was the prime avatar for Terra, the Greater Titan of the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:34:22-07:00","id":1394778,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I didn\u2019t know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:36:55-07:00","id":1394779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1394778#post1394778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I didn\u2019t know that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm also not sure of her primordial status in 2nd edition. I admit that I've only skimmed through my copies of Origin and Hero to get to the good stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:41:56-07:00","id":1394780,"title":"","content":"I assumed she was a Primordial cause she was Zeus\u2019s grandmother and because she was generally seen as benign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:42:26-07:00","id":1394781,"title":"","content":"The mother of the Titans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:45:55-07:00","id":1394782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1394780#post1394780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed she was a Primordial cause she was Zeus\u2019s grandmother and because she was generally seen as benign.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, just going by what I remember about Greek mythology, I believe the Primordials are supposed to be the embodiment of conceptual forces such as Chaos and Order. While the Titans are more grounded in nature, such as Fire and Water.<br /> <br /> Gaia is the spirit of earth, while her husband Uranus is the spirit of heaven (the sky). While this makes her immensely powerful, I don't think it quite equals the power of a universal concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","user":"NewNyrufa","date":". 06-07-2020, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T09:36:28-07:00","id":1394789,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Interesting point. Thanks. Maybe Titanomachy will clarify this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:12:05-07:00","id":1394799,"title":"","content":"Gaia is a Primordial, the primordial of primordials to the Theoi, as she is the self pregnant Mother of Uranus and T\u00e1rtaro (and many more)<br /> <br /> She is not benign, she went for a revanche against the gods for killing her Titans, releasing the Gigantes, that started the Gigantomachia.<br /> <br /> On the benign/malign thing, most of the ancient culture have a very opened way to deal on good and bad, the Theoi for example are not good or bad, they just have their things to do that may or not involve killing people for no or meaningless reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 06-07-2020, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:36:12-07:00","id":1394807,"title":"","content":"In 2e I'd make Gaia a Primordial, yeah. See my previous post on page 1 about the 1e Titan Cosmology being Dumb and Reductionist and Best Thrown In A Bin (setting it on fire after is optional but I'd do it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T10:53:43-07:00","id":1394818,"title":"","content":"I suppose if Gaia is supposed to represent the World (capital W) and not just the planet earth, then being a Primordial would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","user":"NewNyrufa","date":". 06-07-2020, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:29:51-07:00","id":1394825,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz, Kyman201 I agree with you guys. I think Gaia works better as a Primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:30:23-07:00","id":1394826,"title":"","content":"I meant <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:31:49-07:00","id":1394827,"title":"","content":"No worries, I don't actually need to be tagged every time I'm mentioned. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T04:52:57-07:00","id":1395053,"title":"","content":"Considering that Gaia is still an active player in the World game of the Theoi, I wouldn't consider her as a Primordial. She does still want to dethrone Zeus, and while she kinda of gave up for a while after the Typhon fiasco, as far as am aware she is still willing to do so. Also, she does still have new children which interfere with the World, like with Poseidon she had Antaeus who fought Herakles.<br /> <br /> I see her more as a Titan of Fertility in the Motherhood aspect, and while allied and friendly with the Theoi, she is a proven and dangerous potential hostile, just waiting for a good chance to bring on Typhon Episode 2: The attack of the Cyclones. I also think it is kinda of cool to imagine that the heroes in my game might at some point fighting the earth itself, bringing someone who before was friendly and maybe even an actively ally to the ranks of terrifying enemy.<br /> <br /> Also, while I appreciate the overall restructuring for the Titans in 2ed, I think its definition is a bit too unclear and limiting. I hope Titanomachy solves it, but it still makes me feel like the Titans are supposed to be the villains. Like, Bes is a Titan, even if he isn't that particularly different from any of the Thuata, both physically, mentally and in power level. Why is he a Titan, besides the fact that, from the point of the view of the Thuata, he is evil? I don't know of any reason that a Scion of Bes would be any different from a Scion of Lugh or Dagda.<br /> <br /> Prometheus also suffers a bit for that, as this definition simplifies his character too much for my liking. No longer there are questions of why he brought the fire to humanity: did he liked humanity, his own creation, so much that he was willing to maybe suffer under Zeus hatred for them? Did he just wanted to see what happened if humanity had fire, and was willing to suffer for it? As the embodiment of forethought, is this part of a (ridiculously) long game for a bigger plan, maybe for him to become the king of the Cosmos itself? Nope, he just really wanted humanity to &quot;create&quot;, as a Titan of Creativity.<br /> <br /> Titans and Gods aren't really that different in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T05:05:21-07:00","id":1395057,"title":"","content":"I prefer to look less at what the titans do themselves in regard to a war against the gods and more how they influence The World.<br /> <br /> Using Gaia as an example, i'm less interested in her trying to overthrow Zeus herself and more on could there be a cult that want her to overthrow Zeus. Or is there a scion going around that people never heard before that Gaia declares to be the &quot;Son of Zeus, destined to overthrow his father&quot; as a part of a plan or something.<br /> <br /> The Mortal World is also the &quot;level&quot; where i prefer to have my mix and match of antagonist from varying mythologies.<br /> <br /> A bit of an aside tho, Prometheus isnt a titan of Creativity he is Foresight. So whatever reason he had for doing what he did for humanity, he knew what was going to happen. Which i find to be an amazing fodder for story ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I want to run a game where all the chaos and danger the scions meet turns up being a sorta friendly mastermind chessmatch between Prometheus of Foresight and Utgard-Loki of Illusions.<br /> With the pcs as both pawns but also spanners in the work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T05:21:13-07:00","id":1395059,"title":"","content":"That is an interesting point of view, especially considering that right now any Titan war is far above anything heroes can do. And definitely in the World would be people wanting to overthrow Zeus, he can be very unpopular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1395057#post1395057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of an aside tho, Prometheus isnt a titan of Creativity he is Foresight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but they say &quot;Prometheus is creativity&quot; in the book (Scion: Hero, pg. 15, second paragraph under TITANS). I presume to associate him with Fire (creativity) as the Purview and easily explain why the god of Foresight (or Forethought, the difference is splitting hairs) would do such a thing. Plus, I don't know how Foresight would fit in the Purviews.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just to add, in the line just before that, in the same paragraph, they also say that he wasn't overcome by compassion to humans, and the line after that it says it was &quot;a inevitability&quot;, further exemplifying my point that Titans seem to be too simplistic, as far as their characterization goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 06-08-2020, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T14:05:18-07:00","id":1395144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1395059#post1395059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but they say &quot;Prometheus is creativity&quot; in the book (Scion: Hero, pg. 15, second paragraph under TITANS). I presume to associate him with Fire (creativity) as the Purview and easily explain why the god of Foresight (or Forethought, the difference is splitting hairs) would do such a thing. Plus, I don't know how Foresight would fit in the Purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are points in Scion's first chapter that I choose to ignore, such as the parts that mention Exemplars and a unified nature for what makes Titans or Primordials.<br /> <br /> Which are things that it seem like the Pantheon writers flat-out ignore as well, if you look at them. I figure that there were different writers.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;How would that fit in the Purviews&quot;... Well it might not. In the Purviews we have.<br /> <br /> But in that case, I'd just make a new one. I saw someone musing on making an Insight Purview, for the Gods who are quite famously All-Seeing, and that one probably would make sense for Prometheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:30:38-07:00","id":1395288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1395144#post1395144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in that case, I'd just make a new one. I saw someone musing on making an Insight Purview, for the Gods who are quite famously All-Seeing, and that one probably would make sense for Prometheus.</div> </div> </div> </div>God, an Insight Purview sounds like an excellent idea! I've always felt something was missing there. Do you know if anybody is currently working on this?<br /> <br /> And on the main topic of discussion: personally, I hope that future supplements move away from the idea that Titans have only one associated Purview. That seems like a holdover from 1e. It makes sense for some Titans (like Surtr, maybe) and I can see how having a relatively simple villain figure can be useful, especially at lower Tiers. But as the game begins to move into the more cosmic Tiers of Demigod and God, I don't see why, say, the Fomorians should be any less complicated then their rivals, the Tuatha D\u00e9. And that's not even going into the idea of playing Titanic Scions. For me at least, it tends to make the Titans a bit too single-minded and not all that interesting as opponents. Especially if you are interested in an overarching Titanomachy, I think defining Titans by their one Purview isn't very useful to think about their broader motives as antagonists and why some of them might band together against the Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T04:12:46-07:00","id":1395293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Wopsle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1391093-second-titan-war?p=1395288#post1395288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God, an Insight Purview sounds like an excellent idea! I've always felt something was missing there. Do you know if anybody is currently working on this?<br /> <br /> And on the main topic of discussion: personally, I hope that future supplements move away from the idea that Titans have only one associated Purview. That seems like a holdover from 1e. It makes sense for some Titans (like Surtr, maybe) and I can see how having a relatively simple villain figure can be useful, especially at lower Tiers. But as the game begins to move into the more cosmic Tiers of Demigod and God, I don't see why, say, the Fomorians should be any less complicated then their rivals, the Tuatha D\u00e9. And that's not even going into the idea of playing Titanic Scions. For me at least, it tends to make the Titans a bit too single-minded and not all that interesting as opponents. Especially if you are interested in an overarching Titanomachy, I think defining Titans by their one Purview isn't very useful to think about their broader motives as antagonists and why some of them might band together against the Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Insight Purview is, IMO, one of the few holes left in the Purview set, and would be an excellent addition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I definitely agree about divorcing Titans from the single Purview idea... honestly, I'm more leaning into the idea that Titan should be an entirely political divide at this point... after all, we know Gods will be able to have Titanic Callings, there will be some in Demigod who do so, and at this point you might as well just give titans the 3 Callings + Purviews treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:08:36-07:00","id":1395307,"title":"","content":"I see an Insight Purview as a grand replacement for Epic Perception and Epic Intelegence (I suppose the Cunning Purview replaces Epic Wits). Still many deities are gods of Wisdom or a similar trait. This is a needed Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}